  "networkNotes": "A real-road network (run W-S; interview, 2026-10-02: map-based networks, multi-lane highways, junction choices): the Overseas Highway (US 1) four lanes wide over Stock Island and Cow Key Channel into Key West, then South Roosevelt Boulevard along Smathers Beach, Bertha Street and Atlantic Boulevard to Higgs Beach; North Roosevelt Boulevard leaves at the Triangle and comes back down Truman Avenue and White Street, about the same distance. Its own frame origin, since it never shares a scene with keys-m1. Junction pieces and connector roads are synthesized; the lines are pinned to the real junctions (closure). Playtest 4 (P4-19, B5): the two Martello forts are landmarks of the line, East Martello on South Roosevelt Boulevard by the airport and West Martello at Higgs Beach (`keys-landmarks#east_martello` and `#west_martello`), each on the sea side past the verge and drawn at 0.47 and 0.7 of the model's size so the box stands on the 24 m of land. They were placed by hand in the baked roads and in these entries, not re-baked (no OSM extract was at hand), at coordinates remembered, not checked against a map: each `at` is the box's centre taken from the baked road's own metres, so a re-bake, which projects the point onto the real polyline, may land a fort elsewhere along its road.",
